  "title": "Safavid Empire",
  "summary": "The Safavids ruled Persia from 1501 to 1722. They began around 1300 as a mystical order centred on Ardabil, and made Shi'ism the state religion, setting the territorial and Shi'ite principles of modern Iran. Shah Abbas I is especially known for encouraging commerce. Revolts and Afghan invasion brought them down, and Shah Husayn's forced abdication in 1722 ended their rule.",
